  "reads": [
    "Sub-threshold rungs are seed-robust too: scale 1 sits at the grad-norm variance floor (fire ~0.85-2.6x, no genuine fire), scale 2 and 4 fire (fire ~11-25x and ~34-78x) but all 3 seeds RECOVER (transient) \u2014 the fire ratio climbs monotonically with amplitude and the transient band reproduces across seeds.",
    "INVERSE lead/severity coupling is seed-stable across ~7 runaway rungs x 3 seeds (not n=2 on one seed): median lead 8->11, 10->7, 12->6, 14->6, 16->5, 24->4, 32->4 \u2014 monotone non-increasing, spread <=4 steps.",
    "The lead FLOORS at ~4 steps (earliest NaN is step 304, 4 after burst onset 300) even at a 32x shock \u2014 it does NOT shrink to 0; the warning window has a hard floor set by the compounding steps needed to overflow.",
    "scale 6 is the transient->runaway KNIFE-EDGE and is seed-fragile: 1/3 seeds runs away (lead 70, slow tail overflow @370), 2/3 recover \u2014 the operating-envelope threshold made concrete (lead longest + stochastic AT threshold, floored deep past it)."
  ]
